# .git is deliberately NOT ignored: setuptools_scm derives the version from it,
# and the build fails without it.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.log

# `.github/` and `wiki/` are NOT ignored, and that is deliberate. Both are
# tracked — wiki/ as a gitlink — so leaving them out of the context while `.git`
# stays in it makes git inside the build see deleted files, call the tree dirty,
# and setuptools_scm then bumps PAST the tag: v0.2.0 shipped an image whose
# /info reported 0.2.1.dev0+gd5bf435d4.d20260916.
#
# They cost nothing to carry. In CI the wiki submodule is not checked out, so it
# is an empty directory, and `.github/` is a handful of YAML that lands in the
# final COPY layer — after the dependency layer that actually takes the time.

# The built UI (npm --prefix ui run build). Generated, never committed (§F4.15).
kubed/selenium_flow/http/static/
ui/node_modules/
